    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "4.\nAPR 23\n4 PM.\nCALLE\nHYES\nFROM\nPan American Airways, Inc.,\nHONOLULO, H. I., U. S. A.\nFIRST FLIGHT\nPAN AMERICAN CLIPPER\nHAWAI CAR-ORNIA\nAFR 22\n2 P!\nHAWAI\nCh\nOAHU\nCHES\n193\nUNTU\nHDSYVVVRSROSTAGB\nANCISCO\nAPRE\n- 2- Pivi\n7935\nTO\nRobert C. Kipp\n400 W. Grove St.\nGreenville, Mich.\nPAN AMERICAN CLIPPER M\nFURST FLIGHT\nCALIFORNIA-HAWAN",
      "ROBERT C. KIPP\n400 W. GROVE ST.\nGREENVILLE, MICH.\nMar 30,1935\nOn this day t am sending for a\ntrans Pacific flight cover. this flight\nIs not authorzes by the Philatdic\nagency because it holds no contract\nover the route to be flown. the Pan\nAmerican Airways, Inc. is handling\nthis plight they changes foca round\ntrip. Dad gover me the money the\nnight of the Father and ton Ranguet.\nRobert Conrad Kipp."
